lcos-updates (0.9-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Cancelling a check while kept-back packages are classified says the
    check was cancelled. A probe that does not succeed is not described as
    needing extra packages.
  * A maintainer-script failure keeps dpkg's detail line. An unpack or
    configure failure says the upgrade stopped with a package unfinished.
  * Kept-back classification has a short budget inside the check deadline,
    shows "Checking kept-back packages…", and does not call unprobed names
    extra packages.
  * Apt update and install pass quiet=0 so download percents reach the
    window. The last progress line is shown when apt exits.
  * A check shows how much will be downloaded.
  * Configuring names the package. After dpkg goes idle the note says
    downloading.
  * A hidden install notifies at 10 minutes without progress, and again
    when shutdown is no longer blocked.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0000

lcos-updates (0.9-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Closing after an install that already finished reports that result and
    does not leave Check stuck. The same outcome text is used for the
    window and the notification.
  * A finished install keeps phased, held, and kept-back packages from the
    check, and says "You're up to date" only when nothing is left.
  * Once dpkg has started, the install is not killed for idle time or the
    hard cap. A stall shows how long the phase has run, and after a long
    stall the shutdown inhibitor is relaxed.
  * Package-list errors keep apt's own lines. A proxy or offline hint is
    added only when that cause is plausible.
  * A full disk shows dpkg's cause. dpkg --configure -a is mentioned only
    after an interrupted dpkg has exited.
  * A restart sentence is printed once, after "Updates installed." A
    reboot-required flag that was already there is not called this install.
  * A package kept back because another package would be removed is
    described as a removal.
  * Apt's carriage-return download progress is shown in the window.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:40:00 +0000

lcos-updates (0.9-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A package-list refresh that fetched nothing is an error, not "up to
    date". A partial refresh (some indexes arrived) still continues, and
    that warning is shown above the result.
  * Once dpkg has started unpacking or configuring, Cancel is disabled and
    the install runs to completion. Closing the window hides it and a
    notification reports the real outcome. Before that phase, Cancel and
    Close still stop the job.
  * Phased updates and held packages are named for what they are. A
    name:arch pin is accepted, and a refused pin is named.
  * The apt capture keeps the summary, kept-back and phasing sections, and
    conffile notes. A missing summary is not reported as up to date.
  * Apt's idle clock restarts while output is still arriving. The window
    shows the phase and the last apt line. A hard cap still applies.
  * Logout and shutdown are inhibited when the session provides a way.
    Otherwise the install window says not to log out or shut down.
  * A reboot-required flag after install says to restart and names the
    packages.
  * Authentication failures name a missing agent, a rejected password, or
    a dismissed dialog. The password wait says it is waiting, and times
    out on its own.
  * The status area scrolls so a long error leaves the buttons on screen.
    The action buttons have mnemonics, and Escape cancels before dpkg.
  * Cancelling a check says so, even after an install timed out.
  * A connection failure says to set a proxy in /etc/apt/apt.conf.d. The
    apt child's environment stays cleared.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 08:10:00 +0000

lcos-updates (0.9-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Only a live dpkg --unpack/--configure/--install/--remove/--triggers-only
    counts as package configuration. Architecture queries, dpkg-query, and
    zombies no longer disable cancel or the deadline, and apt-get update
    never latches. The window keeps its timer, and says "Configuring
    packages…", only while that dpkg is still running.
  * If configuration is already in the tree, the helper waits for apt to exit
    instead of returning while apt and dpkg are still running.
  * Helper errors are one protocol line per line, so a partial index warning
    does not hide the later failure.
  * A stale authentication SIGKILL cannot hit the next pkexec. Closing the
    window cancels a queued check and does not run a nested dialog over the
    helper's child watch.
  * Install upgrades the reviewed package=version list, or shows the new list
    and installs nothing if the post-update simulation differs.
  * Polkit denies inactive and non-local subjects. Install does not keep a
    cached authorization. The window runs /usr/bin/pkexec with no PATH search.
  * Stopping apt records process start times and signals only those pids.
  * The apt child starts from a cleared environment.
  * Kept conffiles are named. The window does not claim the system is up to
    date when an old conffile was kept.
  * dpkg scans are throttled and apt output is capped. Cancel is a button.
    The progress bar stays hidden until the helper is ready. A spawn failure
    is not reported as a missing pkexec, and startup timestamp 0 is rejected.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 19:10:00 +0000

lcos-updates (0.9-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Do not signal dpkg once package configuration has started. Cancel still
    stops apt-get during download. Closing the window while dpkg is running
    warns and leaves the helper running. If a kill already happened, report
    dpkg --configure -a instead of treating that as a clean stop.
  * Kept-back packages and a non-zero "not upgraded" count are not reported
    as up to date. Those packages are named. This tool still will not install
    updates that need extra packages (apt-get upgrade only, not dist-upgrade).
  * A partial apt-get update still runs the upgrade simulation and shows the
    apt warning. Offline wording is only for resolve failures, unreachable
    networks, unable to connect, and connection timeouts.
  * Check and install time limits restart when the helper is ready, so the
    password dialog is not part of the apt budget. Authentication timeouts
    say so.
  * Cancel closes the helper pipe and waits for the child watch. The window
    no longer walks /proc on the UI thread. A zero stop grace does not sleep.
  * Checking again keeps the package list until the new check returns a
    definitive result. Cancel or error puts the rows back and re-enables
    Install.
  * A second launch presents the window with the startup-notification
    timestamp. --check during a job runs when that job finishes.
  * Use the system-software-update icon until hicolor artwork exists. Meson
    skips missing PNG paths.
  * Enter activates Install when the package list is showing, and Check when
    it is hidden.
  * Install runs apt-get update before apt-get upgrade.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 05:42:00 +0000

